    "result": "The implementation is in `solution.py` and the test suite is in `tests/test_solution.py`. `python -m pytest -q tests` passes all 34 tests. I could not run a coverage measurement because only the test command is allowed, so the 90% gate is unverified. By reading the code, every branch in `solution.py` is exercised by a test, so I expect coverage to be near 100%.\n\nThe implementation follows `spec.md` in this order: validate items, then check the coupon, then compute the discount, then apply shipping to the discounted subtotal, and round the final total to cents with ROUND_HALF_UP. Two interpretation choices went beyond the spec text. First, a `bool` quantity is rejected as not an integer. Second, when the coupon is invalid, the `CouponError` checks run before the `ValueError` value checks for the percent and fixed kinds. The signature, the `CouponError` class and the module layout are unchanged. The tests cover each rule, the boundary cases (expiry day, minimum subtotal, the 100.00 free-shipping threshold, percent 100 and 100.01, fixed discounts capped at the subtotal) and a half-up rounding case.",
